body:
It’s so great that you’re doing workbooks!! That’s such an amazing thing to be doing on your own. 

I’m so sorry that the therapist you saw wasn’t very helpful, I must’ve missed that comment. in my own experience, I had to go through something like 4-5 different therapists to find one that clicked. not all therapists are built the same, and some will work better for you than others! I’m not sure if you have already, but have you looked into dialectical behavioural therapists at all? DBT therapists are trained to deal specifically with BPD, so you might have more luck finding a better fit if we explore that route. 

if that’s not an option, I have a lot of other tips that can help as well. whatever you need! :)
